{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "העניק", :translit "ha'anik", :gloss "you shall endowed"} {:he "מלא יו\"ד", :translit "malei yod", :gloss "full with yod"} {:he "ע\"י העשר מכות", :translit "al yedei ha'eser makkot", :gloss "through the ten plagues"} {:he "הענקתיך", :translit "he'anaktikha", :gloss "I endowed you"} {:he "ג' דברים", :translit "sheloshah devarim", :gloss "three things"} {:he "כלי כסף", :translit "klei kesef", :gloss "silver vessels"} {:he "וכלי זהב", :translit "ukhei zahav", :gloss "and gold vessels"} {:he "ושמלות", :translit "vesimlot", :gloss "and garments"} {:he "מצאנך", :translit "mitsonkha", :gloss "from your flock"} {:he "ומגרנך", :translit "umigornkha", :gloss "and from your threshing floor"} {:he "ומיקבך", :translit "umiyikvekha", :gloss "and from your winepress"} {:he "וזכרת כי עבד היית", :translit "vezakharat ki eved hayita", :gloss "and you shall remember that you were a servant"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "העניק", :b "ע\"י העשר מכות"} {:kind :other, :note "Derives the tripartite gift obligation from the three categories Israel received at the Exodus."}], :frame {:text "The full spelling of העניק with a letter yod yields a numerical value identical to ע\"י העשר מכות, 'through the ten plagues.' Israel left Egypt endowed with three categories of wealth — silver vessels, gold vessels, and garments (Exodus 3:22, 11:2, 12:35) — received on account of the ten plagues. Therefore the Hebrew slave must be endowed from three corresponding categories: flock, threshing floor, and winepress (Deuteronomy 15:14). The verse 'and you shall remember that you were a servant' (Deuteronomy 15:15) underscores the reciprocity: just as Israel was enriched upon liberation from servitude, so must one enrich the freed slave. The obligation to give gifts to a freed slave is stated in Deuteronomy 15:14, and the exhortation to remember Israel's own bondage follows in Deuteronomy 15:15.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 15:14" "Deuteronomy 15:15" "Exodus 3:22" "Exodus 11:2" "Exodus 12:35"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "העניק", :a-value 235, :b "ע\"י העשר מכות", :b-value 1121, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Derives the tripartite gift obligation from the three categories Israel received at the Exodus.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:53.688886006Z", :model "glm-5.2"}